# Additional Shared-Directory Improvement

For a team-shared directory, a more controlled approach is to use the **setgid bit**:

```bash
sudo chmod 2775 /opt/team-workspace
```

The `2` sets the setgid bit on the directory.

### Why this is useful

New files and directories created inside the workspace can inherit the directory's group, which is useful for team collaboration.

```text
/opt/team-workspace
        |
        +--- group: project-team
        |
        +--- file1 → project-team
        +--- file2 → project-team
```

This is a useful concept for real-world Linux administration.

